  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Pacific SIDS to identify, protect and manage natural &amp; cultural heritage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen Pacific SIDS&#x2019; capacities to effectively protect, conserve and manage natural and cultural heritage through the implementation of the 1972 Convention Concerning the Protection of the World Cultural and Natural Heritage. The suggested interventions include the implementation of priority actions identified in the Regional Action Plan for World Heritage for the Pacific 2021-2025 (40 C/5 activity) and selected recommendations from the Regional World Heritage Workshop in 2023 (41 C/5 activity). The activities involve supporting regional and national level capacity building; a mentoring scheme in support of national efforts to review and update Tentative List of potential World Heritage Sites; a regional WH collaboration mechanism for the implementation of the Convention and the effective coordination with other relevant organizations; and support links of heritage preservation to sustainable tourism.</narrative>
  </description>
